  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of Early 19th-Century First Baptist Church in Mawlamyine, Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The early 19th-century First Baptist Church in Mawlamyine is a masterful blend of Burmese craft traditions and Western architectural styles. The project, which continues work begun under a previous Ambassadors Fund grant, directly supports the U.S. embassys efforts to promote national reconciliation, respect for religious and ethnic diversity, and training in the detection and safe removal of asbestos in historic buildings.</narrative>
  </description>
